{
  "id": "u09-l06",
  "unit": "u09-past",
  "title": "Was / were",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "In the present, 'is' disappears: **আমি ছাত্র** 'I am a student'. In the past it **comes back** as **ছিল-**:\n\n- আমি **ছিলাম**: I was\n- তুমি **ছিলে**: you were\n- আপনি / তিনি **ছিলেন**: you were / he, she was (polite)\n- সে **ছিল**: he / she / it was\n\n**ছিল-** is also the past of **আছ-**: **আমি বাসায় আছি** → **আমি বাসায় ছিলাম** 'I was at home'.\n\n**গত সপ্তাহে** = 'last week'. **শিক্ষার্থী** is a gender-neutral 'student' (ছাত্র / ছাত্রী mark gender).\n\n**মতো** 'like' comes after a possessive: **সে তার মায়ের মতো** 'She is like her mother'. (Liking something is **পছন্দ**.)\n\n**ছিল** is also written **ছিলো**.",
  "vocab": [
